A_kwDORymbOs4mM1S1","name":"herdr-macos-x86_64","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":24367600,"digest":"sha256:5fb0a908ec7f6745e3e245738b06bfad56c46391c391ab3c0955fbead01f1369","download_count":5044,"created_at":"2026-10-14T16:07:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T16:07:27Z"},{"id":640898234,"node_id":"RA_kwDORymbOs4mM1S6","name":"herdr-windows-x86_64.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":10037141,"digest":"sha256:d2c6c9c971c43a0bfdde8c692a9a1a7a45c3e4807cd01ae45662b4734fac1cbf","download_count":43856,"created_at":"2026-10-14T16:07:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T16:07:26Z"}],"body":"This is a hotfix release for v0.9.4. See the v0.9.4 notes for the full feature release: https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/releases/tag/v0.9.4\n\n### Fixed\n- Prefix shortcuts work again when the terminal sends the next key as plain text. This affected Tern, Chinese, Japanese and Korean input methods on macOS, and Ghostty `text:` keybinds that send the prefix and a key together. Workspace navigation had the same problem. (#5255)\n- Codex sessions no longer start with a \"clamping Interrupt hook timeout\" warning. Herdr no longer installs Codex turn hooks, and Codex status comes from screen detection again. Run `herdr integration install codex` to update. (#5246, #5278)\n- Claude Code questions show as blocked in named sessions. (#4573, #5192)\n- On Windows, plugin panes start even when a folder on `PATH` has the same name as the plugin's program. (#5267, #5269, thanks @JJLiebig)\n- On Windows, Claude Code session tracking works when the user folder name contains non-ASCII characters, such as Korean. (#5253, #5270, thanks @JJLiebig)\n- Adding a Windows machine no longer prints raw PowerShell progress output. (#4639, #5282, thanks @JJLiebig)\n","reactions":{"total_count":16,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":16,"eyes":0},"mentions_count":1}
